<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 1.756 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    345 days   20.98 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days   21.17 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days   20.30 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    700 million     34 days   19.84 pct</p>
<p>    500 million	2 days   18.46 pct</p>
<p>    106 million	1 day    18.45 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
